---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Credits & Attributions" description="Attributions, open source credits, and acknowledgements.">
  <article>
    <h1>Credits & Acknowledgements</h1>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>Visual Palette: Ef Themes</h2>
      <p>
        The color system of this site is directly ported from <strong>ef-themes</strong>,
        a collection of colorful and legible themes for GNU Emacs created by
        <a href="https://protesilaos.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Protesilaos Stavrou</a>.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong><code>ef-autumn</code> (Dark Mode)</strong>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong><code>ef-arcadia</code> (Light Mode)</strong>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong><code>ef-day</code> (Alternate Light Preset)</strong>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        All hexadecimal color values in the CSS stylesheets are 100% faithful to the upstream
        Lisp source definitions in <code>ef-autumn-theme.el</code>, <code>ef-arcadia-theme.el</code>,
        and <code>ef-day-theme.el</code>, released under the GNU General Public License v3.0 or later.
      </p>
    </section>

    <hr />

    <section>
      <h2>Typography</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Headings, Navigation & Monospace</strong> - <strong>Typus Mono 95</strong>,
          a customized monospace typeface created by Szymon Wilczek (me, ;D)
          (<a href="https://github.com/szymonwilczek/typus-fonts" target="_blank" rel="noopener">typus-fonts repository</a>).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Prose & Reading Body</strong> - <em>Source Serif 4</em> (SIL Open Font License)
          paired with <em>Newsreader</em> and <em>Charter</em> for classical print aesthetics.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
